Package: chromstatR
Type: Package
Title: Quantitative Chromatin State Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Helen", "Huang", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "helenhuang.math@gmail.com")
Description: R interface to the ChromState Python package for quantitative chromatin
    state analysis. Fits a joint negative-binomial hidden Markov model across samples,
    then reports per-region soft state composition, call confidence, continuous
    bivalency scores, per-mark attribution of every state call, and state dynamics
    between conditions. Results are returned as GRanges and data frames so they drop
    into existing Bioconductor workflows.
